# ADR-010 (chosen) — Inngest owns Follow-up-plan CONTROL state; the local DB owns OUTPUT state only.
# One canonical store for live workflow state; `nurture_sequences` is dropped.
# House style: render with `d2 --layout elk --theme 0` (neutral light, no sketch).
direction: right

title: |md
  **ADR-010 (chosen)** — Inngest is canonical for run state (one fn per Lead); local DB holds only outputs; `nurture_sequences` dropped
|
title.near: top-center

events: Domain events · via outbox (adr014) {
  style.stroke-dash: 3
  ev: lead.captured · lead.stage-changed
}

inngest: Inngest — CANONICAL control state {
  icon: ./icons/inngest.svg
  runner: "one fn instance per Lead · concurrency {key: leadId, limit: 1} · sleeps to cadence boundary"
  dash: Inngest dashboard · answers operator questions (no admin UI)
}

neon: Neon Postgres — OUTPUT state only {
  icon: ./icons/neon.svg
  leads: leads · canonical Lead row (adr013) {
    shape: cylinder
  }
  mq: message_queue {
    shape: cylinder
  }
  conv: conversations {
    shape: cylinder
  }
  dropped: nurture_sequences · DROPPED + one-per-lead index removed {
    style.stroke-dash: 3
  }
}

dashboard: Consultant dashboard {
  icon: ./icons/nextjs.svg
}

events.ev -> inngest.runner: 1 · consume · spin up / advance runner {
  style: {
    animated: true
    stroke: green
  }
}
inngest.runner -> neon.mq: 2 · insert message_queue · emit nurture.followup-message-drafted
dashboard -> neon.mq: 3 · reads approval queue · joined to leads
dashboard -> neon.conv: reads sent history
inngest.runner -> inngest.dash: operator view — no Rekurve admin UI {
  style.stroke-dash: 3
}
